  "description": "Several security issues were discovered in the Linux kernel.\nAn attacker could possibly use these to compromise the system.\nThis update corrects flaws in the following subsystems:\n  - Multiple devices driver;\n  - eXpress Data Path;\n  - Kernel build system;\n  - ARM64 architecture;\n  - PowerPC architecture;\n  - RISC-V architecture;\n  - S390 architecture;\n  - x86 architecture;\n  - Block layer subsystem;\n  - Intel NPU Driver;\n  - Compute Acceleration Framework;\n  - ACPI drivers;\n  - Drivers core;\n  - Ublk userspace block driver;\n  - Bus devices;\n  - Hardware random number generator core;\n  - Clock framework and drivers;\n  - Clocksource drivers;\n  - Hardware crypto device drivers;\n  - CXL (Compute Express Link) drivers;\n  - Buffer Sharing and Synchronization framework;\n  - DMA engine subsystem;\n  - DPLL subsystem;\n  - EDAC drivers;\n  - FireWire subsystem;\n  - Arm Firmware Framework for ARMv8-A(FFA);\n  - ARM SCMI message protocol;\n  - GPIO subsystem;\n  - GPU drivers;\n  - HID subsystem;\n  - Microsoft Hyper-V drivers;\n  - Hardware monitoring drivers;\n  - CoreSight HW tracing drivers;\n  - I3C subsystem;\n  - InfiniBand drivers;\n  - Input Device core drivers;\n  - Input Device (Mouse) drivers;\n  - IOMMU subsystem;\n  - Media drivers;\n  - MMC subsystem;\n  - Network drivers;\n  - Mellanox network drivers;\n  - Microsoft Azure Network Adapter (MANA) driver;\n  - STMicroelectronics network drivers;\n  - Texas Instruments network drivers;\n  - Ethernet team driver;\n  - MediaTek network drivers;\n  - NTB driver;\n  - NVME drivers;\n  - Operating Performance Points (OPP) driver;\n  - PCI subsystem;\n  - Synopsys DesignWare PCIe PMU;\n  - Pin controllers subsystem;\n  - x86 platform drivers;\n  - i.MX PM domains;\n  - PTP clock framework;\n  - PWM drivers;\n  - Remote Processor subsystem;\n  - S/390 drivers;\n  - SCSI subsystem;\n  - ASPEED SoC drivers;\n  - SoundWire subsystem;\n  - SPI subsystem;\n  - Greybus lights staging drivers;\n  - Realtek RTL8723BS SDIO drivers;\n  - Thermal drivers;\n  - TTY drivers;\n  - UFS subsystem;\n  - USB Gadget drivers;\n  - USB Type-C Port Controller Manager driver;\n  - vDPA drivers;\n  - VFIO drivers;\n  - Virtio Host (VHOST) subsystem;\n  - Framebuffer layer;\n  - ACRN Hypervisor Service Module driver;\n  - Virtio drivers;\n  - Watchdog drivers;\n  - Xen hypervisor drivers;\n  - AFS file system;\n  - BTRFS file system;\n  - Ceph distributed file system;\n  - EROFS file system;\n  - File systems infrastructure;\n  - Ext4 file system;\n  - F2FS file system;\n  - GFS2 file system;\n  - Network file systems library;\n  - Network file system (NFS) client;\n  - Network file system (NFS) server daemon;\n  - NTFS3 file system;\n  - OCFS2 file system;\n  - Overlay file system;\n  - Proc file system;\n  - SMB network file system;\n  - Tracing file system;\n  - XFS file system;\n  - BPF subsystem;\n  - Control group (cgroup);\n  - Memory Management;\n  - MAC80211 subsystem;\n  - KASAN memory debugging framework;\n  - Mellanox drivers;\n  - Networking core;\n  - Netfilter;\n  - Perf events;\n  - Tracing infrastructure;\n  - MediaTek SoC drivers;\n  - RCU subsystem;\n  - userfaultfd() syscall;\n  - Amateur Radio drivers;\n  - Bluetooth subsystem;\n  - Wireless networking;\n  - IPv4 networking;\n  - IPv6 networking;\n  - MultiProtocol Label Switching driver;\n  - Network traffic control;\n  - SCTP protocol;\n  - TCP network protocol;\n  - User-space API (UAPI);\n  - IRQ subsystem;\n  - Scheduler infrastructure;\n  - Timer subsystem;\n  - Memory management;\n  - Ethernet bridge;\n  - CAN network layer;\n  - Ceph Core library;\n  - Ethtool driver;\n  - Handshake API;\n  - IEEE802154.4 network protocol;\n  - IFE protocol;\n  - L2TP protocol;\n  - Packet sockets;\n  - Phonet protocol;\n  - Qualcomm IPC Router (QRTR);\n  - RxRPC session sockets;\n  - SMC sockets;\n  - Network sockets;\n  - Sun RPC protocol;\n  - TIPC protocol;\n  - TLS protocol;\n  - XFRM subsystem;\